  "summary": "A SplitWindow is a window that manages the presentation of two side-by-side view\ncontrollers.\n",
  "description": "The [masterView](api:Titanium.UI.iOS.SplitWindow#masterView) and [detailView](api:Titanium.UI.iOS.SplitWindow#detailView)\nproperties are required before the SplitWindow is opened.\n\nYou use this class to implement a master-detail interface, in which the left-side view presents\na list of items and the right-side presents details of the selected item. The `SplitWindow` is supported\nfor both iPhone and iPad idioms. Use the [Titanium.UI.iOS.createSplitWindow](api:Titanium.UI.iOS#createSplitWindow) method to create a `SplitWindow` object.\n\nThe `SplitWindow` is backed by the native `UISplitViewController` and uses its default behavior:\n\n* In a wide regular width, such as an iPad in landscape, the master view and the detail view are shown side by side.\n* In a narrower regular width, such as an iPad in portrait, the master view is hidden. The display mode button in the\n  navigation bar of the detail view and a swipe from the leading edge show it as an overlay.\n* In a compact width, such as an iPhone in portrait, the split window collapses to a single column and the system\n  navigates between the master view and the detail view.\n\nUse [displayMode](api:Titanium.UI.iOS.SplitWindow#displayMode) and [splitBehavior](api:Titanium.UI.iOS.SplitWindow#splitBehavior)\nto request a different arrangement, [showMasterView](api:Titanium.UI.iOS.SplitWindow#showMasterView) and\n[hideMasterView](api:Titanium.UI.iOS.SplitWindow#hideMasterView) to show or hide the master view, and\n[primaryColumnWidthFraction](api:Titanium.UI.iOS.SplitWindow#primaryColumnWidthFraction) to control its width.\n\nThe system embeds each view in a navigation controller, so the `title` and the navigation bar properties of a\n[Titanium.UI.Window](api:Titanium.UI.Window) apply directly. Set `navBarHidden` to `true` on a window to hide its navigation bar. Use a\n[Titanium.UI.NavigationWindow](api:Titanium.UI.NavigationWindow) as `masterView` or `detailView` to push windows inside a pane.\n\nThe SplitWindow is a top-level window and cannot be contained within another window or view.\n",
  "properties": [
    {
